.TH WSH 1 "September 2026" "Wsh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wsh \- Zsh-compatible shell with interactive defaults
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wsh
.RI [ "Zsh options" ]
.br
.B wsh --doctor
.br
.B wsh --profile
.RB [ --functions ]
.B --
.RI [ "Zsh options" ]
.br
.B wsh --profile-report
.I directory
.br
.B wsh --run
.RB [ --login ]
.B --
.I program
.RI [ arguments... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wsh runs the Zsh language and line editor with history search, autosuggestions,
syntax highlighting and directory jumping. It loads ordinary Zsh startup files.
Existing user configuration and plugins remain supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --doctor
Inspect startup configuration and report duplicate or unverified plugins.
Configuration files are not edited.
.TP
.B --profile
Record startup measurements. Use --functions to include function profiling.
.TP
.B --profile-report
Read a previously saved profile directory.
.TP
.B --run
Run the exact program arguments in the foreground, then return to a prompt.
.TP
.B --wsh-version
Print Wsh version and compiled build identity.
.TP
.B --wsh-help
Print Wsh-specific command usage.
.PP
Wsh options must appear first. Other arguments retain their Zsh meanings;
--version reports the underlying Zsh version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WSH_THEME
Select minimal, wakamex, robbyrussell, agnoster, or a theme definition path.
When unset, the prompt from user configuration is preserved.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.zshrc
Interactive shell configuration, shared with ordinary Zsh.
.TP
.I ~/.z
Directory-jump history, unless ZSHZ_DATA selects another path.
.SH REMOVAL
Change account shells to another installed shell before removing Wsh.
Package removal does not rewrite account records or refuse the transaction.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zsh (1),
.BR chsh (1)
.PP
https://github.com/wakamex/wsh
